  "prompt": "/deep-research NASA has a reference guide for The Space Shuttle that features a detailed look at all the previous Shuttles. Note the shuttle that has the second fewest number of construction milestones listed before 2024. From the flights of the shuttle, create a list of the missions where its landing site was EAFB.",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "NASA has a reference guide for The Space Shuttle that features a detailed look at all the previous Shuttles. Note the shuttle that has the second fewest number of construction milestones listed before 2024. From the flights of the shuttle, create a list of the missions where its landing site was EAFB.",
  "answer": "Based on my research, **Endeavour (OV-105)** has the second fewest construction milestones (10) before 2024, with only Enterprise (9) having fewer.\n\n## Endeavour Missions Landing at Edwards Air Force Base (EAFB)\n\nFrom NASA's official \"Flights of Endeavour\" document, the following 7 missions landed at EAFB:\n\n| Mission | Launch Date | Landing Date | Primary Payload |\n|---------|-------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| **STS-49** | May 7, 1992 | **May 16, 1992 at EAFB** | Rescue, repair, redeploy INTELSAT VI (F-3) |\n| **STS-59** | April 9, 1994 | **April 20, 1994 at EAFB** | Space Radar Laboratory-1 (SRL-1) |\n| **STS-68** | September 30, 1994 | **October 11, 1994 at EAFB** | Space Radar Laboratory-2 (SRL-2) |\n| **STS-67** | March 2, 1995 | **March 18, 1995 at EAFB** | Astro-2 |\n| **STS-100** | April 19, 2001 | **May 1, 2001 at EAFB** | ISS Mission — SSRMS (Canadarm2), MPLM Raffaello, UHF Antenna |\n| **STS-111** | June 5, 2002 | **June 19, 2002 at EAFB** | ISS Mission — Mobile Remote Service Base System, MPLM Leonardo |\n| **STS-126** | November 14, 2008 | **November 30, 2008 at EAFB** | ISS Mission — MPLM Leonardo |\n\n**Total: 7 EAFB landings** out of 25 total Endeavour flights (STS-134 was scheduled but not yet flown at time of this document).\n\n## Sources\n- NASA \"The Space Shuttle\" Reference Guide (construction milestones): https://www.nasa.gov/reference/the-space-shuttle\n- NASA \"Flights of Endeavour\" PDF: https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/2011.05.09-endeavour.pdf",
  "answer_chars": 1507,
  "expected_answer": "STS-49, STS-59, STS-68, STS-67, STS-100, STS-111, STS-126",
